# The time slacks somebody derived rather than measured. One row per layer filing its time
# buffer as a `clearance` derivation, beside the window that would have to license it.
#
# What the derivation assumes
#   `clearance` says the time slack is the clearance, `n - d` read as a quantity in the layer's
#   unit. Reading that quantity as a wait, `q / clearance`, assumes the spare is spread
#   evenly across the denominator.
#
# A stated window says it is not
#   A machine running 02:00 to 05:00 has its spare concentrated, so dividing by the whole period
#   computes over a base that does not exist. `unmeasured` is worse than a stated window, because
#   it hides the same assumption behind a number.
-- pm:Layer/pm:timeSlack filed as a clearance derivation, beside pm:Divisibility/pm:window.
SELECT w.filing, w.layer, w.window_low, w.window_unit, w.window_absent
FROM      (
    :compose(layers/windows.sqlc)
) w
JOIN      (
    :compose(entries/slacks.sqlc)
) s USING (filing, layer)
WHERE s.buffer = 'time' AND s.derivation = 'clearance'
